dnl Practical design goal: deterministic local output suitable for Termux automation.
dnl No network access is required for the module demonstration.
dnl Generated state belongs under $HOME/Language Project rather than inside the Git checkout.
dnl A package being present does not automatically make a benchmark worker active; device verification remains mandatory.
dnl Inputs should be treated as data unless the user explicitly invokes a trusted source execution command.
dnl Use SHA-256 when persistent integrity is required; custom fingerprints remain supplemental.
dnl Prefer atomic temporary-file replacement for any future implementation that modifies user data.
dnl Keep stdout predictable so the module can be composed with other Language Project tools.
dnl Return failures explicitly rather than silently accepting malformed or inaccessible inputs.
dnl Record runtime/compiler versions in reproducible reports where the language participates in benchmarking.
dnl Keep examples small enough for phones while still exercising the real interpreter/compiler.
dnl Avoid root-only behavior so the module remains compatible with ordinary unrooted Termux installations.
